<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    DEEP_TRIBES_FIRE_RITE_1 — what a Deep Tribes harvester does while the rite's
    burn is standing. Assigned by LordToil_RUT_RiteHarvest, never by XML.

    Shape copied from Core's Duties_NonPlayerHome.xml DefendBase: a
    ThinkNode_Priority whose subnodes are tried in order, ending in a wander so
    the duty always produces SOMETHING and the pawn never stands idle waiting
    for the think tree to fall through to a default.

    Order matters and is deliberate:
      1. JobGiver_SeekSafeTemperature — vanilla. This is the "safe standoff from
         the front" the sheet asks for, and it is reused rather than rewritten:
         a harvester standing in air the burn has made lethal leaves before it
         considers picking anything up.
      2. The harvest itself. Refuses any pod in a burning cell, so the party
         works behind the front rather than in it.
      3. JobGiver_WanderNearDutyLocation — vanilla. The radius comes from the
         duty (PawnDuty.wanderRadius, set by the toil), not from here, so the
         one number lives in PyrelandsTuning with the rest of the kit.
  -->
  <DutyDef>
    <defName>RUT_RiteHarvest</defName>
    <thinkNode Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="JobGiver_SeekSafeTemperature" />
        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.PyrelandsMechanics.JobGiver_RUT_HarvestScorchFruit" />
        <li Class="JobGiver_WanderNearDutyLocation">
          <locomotionUrgencyOutsideRadius>Walk</locomotionUrgencyOutsideRadius>
        </li>
      </subNodes>
    </thinkNode>
  </DutyDef>

</Defs>
